{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.874, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:09.348Z", "t_ms": 6825, "delta": "Both **Toolformer** and **Gorilla** train language models to invoke APIs by generating specialized"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.146, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:09.618Z", "t_ms": 7095, "delta": " datasets and fine-tuning base models, but they use fundamentally different learning paradigms and target different API scopes.\n\n---\n\n### Tool"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.318, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:09.793Z", "t_ms": 7270, "delta": "former: Self-Supervised Learning to Call Tools\nToolformer teaches a language model to decide *when*, *which*, and *how*"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.68, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:10.058Z", "t_ms": 7535, "delta": " to call APIs in a self-supervised manner using only a handful of demonstrations per API [C2].\n\n1. **API"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.753, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:10.227Z", "t_ms": 7704, "delta": " Call Representation:** Toolformer formats calls as text sequences demarcated by special tokens: `e(c) = <API> a"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.885, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:10.345Z", "t_ms": 7822, "delta": "_c(i_c) </API>`, where $a_c$ is the API name and $i_"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.389, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:10.803Z", "t_ms": 8279, "delta": "c$ is the input argument [C3]. When executed, the response $r$ is appended after an arrow token: `e("}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.486, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:10.961Z", "t_ms": 8437, "delta": "c, r) = <API> a_c(i_c) -> r </API>` [C3]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.602, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:11.075Z", "t_ms": 8552, "delta": "\n2. **Sampling Candidate Calls:** Starting with a plain text corpus, the model uses in-context learning prompts to"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.804, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:11.279Z", "t_ms": 8756, "delta": " identify candidate positions where an API call might be useful, generating up to $m$ candidate calls per position [C3"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.096, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:11.570Z", "t_ms": 9046, "delta": ", C4].\n3. **Execution and Loss Filtering:** Toolformer executes each candidate call to obtain its result [C3,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.518, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:11.913Z", "t_ms": 9390, "delta": " C4]. It evaluates whether the call and its response reduce the language modeling loss for predicting future tokens compared to doing no"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.638, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:12.111Z", "t_ms": 9588, "delta": " call or receiving no output [C3, C5]. Calls are kept only if the reduction in loss meets or exceeds a filtering"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.889, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:12.363Z", "t_ms": 9840, "delta": " threshold $\\tau_f$ [C5].\n4. **Fine-Tuning:** The surviving API calls are inserted into the original text"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.038, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:12.513Z", "t_ms": 9990, "delta": ", and the language model is fine-tuned on this augmented dataset using a standard language modeling objective [C3, C"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.156, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:12.631Z", "t_ms": 10107, "delta": "6].\n5. **Inference Execution:** During decoding, when the model generates the `->` token, decoding"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.438, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:12.898Z", "t_ms": 10374, "delta": " pauses, the API is invoked, and generation resumes once the response and `</API>` token are appended [C6].\n\n---"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.65, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 44, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:13.118Z", "t_ms": 10594, "delta": "\n\n### Gorilla: Instruction Fine-Tuning with Massive APIs and Document Retrieval\nGorilla focuses on enabling models to use massive, functional"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.052, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 45, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:13.429Z", "t_ms": 10905, "delta": " ML hub APIs (e.g., HuggingFace, Torch Hub, TensorFlow Hub) and pairs fine-tuning with document"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.139, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 46, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:13.613Z", "t_ms": 11089, "delta": " retrieval [C1, C7].\n\n1. **Curating Structured API Documentation:** Gorilla collected model cards across Hug"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.298, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 47, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:13.772Z", "t_ms": 11249, "delta": "gingFace, Torch Hub, and TensorFlow Hub, filtering poorly documented models down to 1,645 APIs [C7]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.562, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 48, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:14.035Z", "t_ms": 11512, "delta": " Each was formatted into a structured JSON object detailing fields like domain, framework, functionality, API name, arguments, code examples"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.768, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 49, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:14.241Z", "t_ms": 11718, "delta": ", and environment requirements [C7].\n2. **Synthetic Instruction Generation:** Following the self-instruct framework, GPT"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.984, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 50, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:14.457Z", "t_ms": 11934, "delta": "-4 was prompted with in-context examples and reference API documentation to generate realistic user instructions without leaking API names or hints, yielding"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 12.163, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 51, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:14.634Z", "t_ms": 12110, "delta": " instruction–API pairs for training [C7, C8].\n3. **Fine-Tuning and Retrieval Integration"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 12.498, "data": {"request_id": "2c869c875a82", "seq": 52, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:16:14.972Z", "t_ms": 12448, "delta": ":** Gorilla fine-tunes a LLaMA base model on this dataset to output precise API calls and arguments [C1]. In addition"}}
